    &\hspace{1.5cm}  + (0.35 {\Delta\phi_{jj}} + 0.18 {x_{h}}) (-0.60 {x_{j_2}} - 0.66 {\Delta\phi_{jj}} - 0.36 {x_{h}}) \nonumber\\
    &\hspace{1.5cm} + 0.42 \cos(0.50 {x_{j_2}} - 1.3 {\Delta\phi_{jj}} + 0.46 {x_{h}})\Big] \notag \\
    & + 0.62 \cos \Big[ 0.50 {x_{j_2}} - 1.3 {\Delta\phi_{jj}} + 0.46 {x_{h}} \Big] \;.
\end{align}
%
Even though it discriminates the SM data better from the $\cHWtil = \pm 1$ cases, it is not \cpo, so a deviation from the SM based on this observable is not a unique sign of \cp violation.

