In addition to the extension to constrained patterns, we relax the linearity assumption of dividends of $\ominus$ over constrained patterns, i.e., we no longer assume the linearity of dividends, while the linearity is assumed for the extended complement algorithm:
For $\CTerm{s}{\phi} \ominus \CTerm{t}{\psi}$, only the dvisor $t$ is assumed to be linear;
for $P \ominus Q$, both $P,Q$ are assumed to be sets of constrained linear patterns.
