In the rest of the paper, for a signature $\Sigma$, we are interested in defined symbols and constructors without an LCTRS $\cR$ which splits $\Sigma$ to $\cD_\cR$ and $\cC_\cR$.
For this reason, without specifying $\cR$, we often split a signature $\Sigma$ to the sets $\cD,\cC$ of defined symbols and constructors, respectively: $\Sigma = \cD \uplus \cC$.

