The set 
%$\{ \symb{f}(\symb{nil},\symb{1}), \symb{f}(\symb{cons}(x',\var{xs}'),\symb{0}), \, \symb{f}(\symb{cons}(x',\var{xs}'),\symb{1}) \}$
$\{ \symb{f}(\symb{nil},\symb{1}), $ $\symb{f}(\symb{cons}(x',\var{xs}'),y) \}$
is a complement of $\symb{f}(\symb{nil},\symb{0})$.
\end{example}

Next, we recall the constructions of complements of linear $\cC$-terms and $\cC$-substitutions.
We follow the formulation in~\cite{HA19pro}.
