% \end{itemize}
For a linear term $u:\iota$, $\Cocterm[\cC]{u}$ is a finite complement of $u$
(i.e., 
% $\{ t \in T(\cC) \mid t:\iota\} = \GInst[\cC]{u} \uplus \GInst[\cC]{\Cocterm[\cC]{u}}$ 
$\GInst[\cC]{\Cocterm[\cC]{u}} = \{ t \in T(\cC) \mid t:\iota\} \setminus \GInst[\cC]{u}$),
which is a set of linear $\cC$-terms.
% (see Proposition~\ref{prop:Cocterms-correctness}).

