\paragraph{Reasoning analysis ranking}
We conduct a tournament-style evaluation of reasoning outputs using \texttt{Doubao-1.5-thinking-pro} as the judge. Only large-sized models with recall scores above 60\% are included in the competition. To avoid order bias, each pair of models competes in two matches: one where model A is evaluated against model B, and another with the order reversed (model B v.s. model A).
This setup yields a total of 1800 competitions among five LLMs. As shown in Table~\ref{tab:tournament-reasoning}, \texttt{GPT-o1} and \texttt{DeepSeek-r1} leads the ranking with 647 and 603 wins, respectively. \texttt{GPT-4o} shows moderate performance, while \texttt{Llama-3.1-405b-instruct} lags far behind. 

