\section{Conclusion}
We present MoDA, a two-stage multimodal diffusion architecture specifically designed for one-shot talking-head synthesis. Our method effectively leverages multimodal information to map audio signals to motion sequences in an identity-agnostic latent space, followed by a dedicated face generator to produce high-quality videos. MoDA can synthesize natural and coherent talking head videos from a single portrait image with high efficiency, while also supporting fine-grained expression control. It significantly outperforms previous state-of-the-art methods in terms of video quality, motion diversity, and naturalness.
