The last measure, $\beta$, is almost fully correlated with network size ($N$). The value of $r_s$ remains below -0.98 for all aggregations except $\Phi_\infty$, where it reaches nearly -0.94. This indicates that, although symmetric vertices are present in the analysed food webs, they do not substantially increase the number of automorphisms in the corresponding automorphism groups.


