We first present a lemma for uniformly convergence of empirical distribution with $\alpha$-mixing data from \cite[Corollary 2.1]{CR92}.

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:alpha-dis}
Let $\{X^{(k)}\}_{k \ge 1}$ be a stationary $\alpha$-mixing sequence of real-valued random variables with distribution $F$ and mixing coefficient $\alpha(m)$ satisfying 
\begin{equation}\label{eq:alpha}
\sum_{m=1}^ \infty m^{-1} (\log m) (\log \log m)^{1+\delta} \alpha(m) < \infty~~~\mbox{for some}~~~\delta>0
\end{equation}
and let $\wF^{N}$ be the empirical d.f. based on the $X^{(1)}, \dots, X^{(N)}$.
 Then, $$\sup_{x \in \R} \vert \wF(x) -F(x)\vert  \to 0, ~~~\p\text{-a.s.}$$
\end{lemma}

